      "content": "it just feels like we're being forced to participate in a play that’s already been canceled. we’re just performing for an empty theater. if there is no ultimate destination and no inherent meaning, then the lutter to find \"purpose\" in suffering just feels like another layer of unnecessary pain. isn't there a certain kind of dignity in just accepting the void? like, if nothing matters, then maybe the only way to truly reclaim control from a meaningless universe is to decide when you've had enough. why is it so wrong to think that stopping the struggle is actually the most logical response to a universe that doesn't care?",
